#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Control panel for the bdex-framegen Vulkan layer.

The layer is an *implicit* Vulkan layer: once installed it loads into every
Vulkan game automatically and stays a pure pass-through until it is turned on.
This window is where you turn it on — like Lossless Scaling, you open it once,
flip frame generation on (globally or for a chosen list of games), set the
quality options, and then launch your games normally through Steam. No Steam
launch options to edit.

Everything here is stored in the layer's config file
(~/.config/bdex-framegen.conf); the layer reads it on its own, so changes take
effect the next time a game starts.

Depends only on Python 3 and PyGObject with GTK 4 and libadwaita (packages
python-gobject, gtk4, libadwaita on most distributions).
"""
